Content-Type: text/plain; charset="us-ascii"

Dear Iryna,

I hope this letter finds you well. As today is your last day with Intellis, I wanted to take a moment to express my heartfelt gratitude and wish you the very best of luck.

From the moment you joined Intellis, you have been an invaluable member of our team. Your dedication and hard work on the Foundation and oCPDS projects have made a significant impact. Your responsibilities on the Foundation project included coordinating with Andrii and ensuring that all tasks were completed efficiently. Additionally, you played a crucial role in testing the mobile application, ensuring its functionality and user experience. On the oCPDS project, you were instrumental in managing test plans, performing exhaustive testing on documentation features, improving the QA process, and ensuring the quality of our deliverables.

Your contributions have not gone unnoticed. You have consistently demonstrated a high level of professionalism and expertise, and your efforts have greatly enhanced our projects. Your ability to manage multiple responsibilities and deliver high-quality work has set a standard for excellence within our team. Furthermore, your commitment to continuous learning and additional training has been commendable.

As you move forward, I want you to know that your presence will be greatly missed. Your positive attitude, dedication, and hard work have made a lasting difference, and I am confident that you will continue to excel in all your future endeavors.

Thank you once again for everything you have done for Intellis. I wish you all the best in your new role and look forward to hearing about your continued success.

Warm regards,
Carmen Macias
Director of Project Management, Group Product Manager at Intellis

